WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.860
A lot of my meeting time went to sharing ideas and discussing them.

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.010
The decision usually waited for the next meeting.

3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.380
I used to ask one person at a time, and I got back one person's experience.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.140
But I wanted more than one way to think about it before I decided.

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:25.900
So I built a team of AI experts. Twenty-five of them. I call on the ones a decision needs.

6
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.210
This is one recorded session. Nothing in it is staged.

7
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:40.820
This time, it was what my training course should teach first.

8
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:45.550
What comes back is a few ways to proceed, and the reason behind each one.

9
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.370
Marcus, the skeptic, checks claims. AI-Joe checks voice.

10
00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:57.890
I own the call.

11
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.890
Fewer of my decisions wait for the next meeting.

12
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.760
You can build your own team and hear it argue, before you decide.

13
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:21.350
Claude did the video editing under my direction, and I approved every cut. The voice and the face are mine.

14
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.690
See how it works at joepointer dot com.
